{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עלה נעלה", :translit "alah na'aleh", :gloss "we shall go up [we shall surely go up]"} {:he "בה\"א", :translit "baheh", :gloss "with a heh"} {:he "סולמות", :translit "sulamot", :gloss "ladders"} {:he "רקיע", :translit "rakia", :gloss "firmament"} {:he "ת\"ק", :translit "tak", :gloss "500"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The repeated verb עלה נעלה uses a heh at the start of the second occurrence rather than the expected וו conjunctive (ונעלה), signaling heightened resolve."}], :frame {:text "Calev's declaration uses a heh prefix on the second verb instead of the expected vav, intensifying the verbal repetition into absolute resolve. The image of ascending to the rakia by ladder echoes Jacob's ladder (Genesis 28:12). The measure that the rakia is a journey of 500 years is found in rabbinic cosmology (Chagigah 13a). The hostile figure addressed as Esav draws on the identification of Esav as the archetypal adversary of Israel.", :sources ["Genesis 28:12" "Chagigah 13a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The repeated verb עלה נעלה uses a heh at the start of the second occurrence rather than the expected וו conjunctive (ונעלה), signaling heightened resolve.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:47.856661899Z", :model "glm-5.2"}